["RHODE ISLAND GROWTH ANALYSES USING PSAT\n\n Damian W Betebenner\n National Center for the Improvement of Educational Assessment\n Providence, Rhode Island May 15th, 2018","BACKGROUND\n\n• Rhode Island’s switch from PARCC to RI-CAS/PSAT10/SAT leads to\n changes in the way that growth is calculated.\n\n• In general, SGPs are using a students’ current test scores combined with at\n least one prior test score subject to the condition that scores come from\n the same test taken at the same time.\n\n• That is, test transitions like those happening in Rhode Island do not\n prevent the calculation of growth. However, communicating how growth is\n calculated across a test transition can be more difficult.\n\n• This presentation provides an overview of due diligence analyses\n conducted for PARCC to PSAT10.","BACKGROUND\n\n• Despite the versatility of SGP analyses not requiring a common scale\n across years, problems can arise with analyses.\n\n• The most common problems are related to ceiling/floor issues on tests as\n well as too few score points on which to calculate the 99 conditional\n quantile curves.\n\n• All source code associated with these analyses (no data) can be found on\n the Center’s GitHub repository for Rhode Island analyses at: https://\n github.com/CenterForAssessment/Rhode_Island","2016 ELA Growth Analyses\n\n 2014 2015 2016\n\n PARCC G3 PARCC G4\n\n PARCC G4 PARCC G5\n\n PARCC G5 PARCC G6\n 2016\n Growth\n Calculations\n PARCC G6 PARCC G7\n\n PARCC G7 PARCC G8\n\n PARCC G8 PARCC G9\n\n PARCC G9 PARCC G10","2016 Mathematics Growth Analyses\n\n 2014 2015 2016\n\n PARCC G3 PARCC G4\n\n PARCC G4 PARCC G5\n\n PARCC G5 PARCC G6\n 2016\n Growth PARCC G6 PARCC G7\n Calculations\n PARCC G7 PARCC G8\n\n PARCC G7 PARCC ALGEBRA I\n\n PARCC G8 PARCC ALGEBRA I\n\n PARCC ALGEBRA I PARCC GEOMETRY","2017 ELA Growth Analyses\n\n 2015 2016 2017\n\n PARCC G3 PARCC G4\n\n PARCC G3 PARCC G4 PARCC G5\n\n PARCC G4 PARCC G5 PARCC G6\n 2017\n Growth PARCC G5 PARCC G6 PARCC G7\n 